Via postman, PATCH to `{{server_url}}/collections/{{collection_name}}`

```
{
    "fields": [
        {
            "name": "embedding",
            "type": "float[]",
            "embed": {
                "from": [
                    "title",
                    "desc",
                    "content"
                ],
                "model_config": {
                    "model_name": "ts/all-MiniLM-L12-v2"
                }
            }
        }
    ]
}
```

PS: I'm afraid I'm guilty of trying to [create an auto-embedding field](https://typesense.org/docs/0.25.2/api/vector-search.html#creating-an-auto-embedding-field) using [update](https://typesense.org/docs/0.25.2/api/collections.html#update-or-alter-a-collection), under the assumption that the change will trigger reindexing, which will then generate the vector field.

As a further note, even restarting the instance hasnt stopped whatever task is going on, on that collection.

@reporter 

On further testing, I'm actually unable to reproduce this issue (it was a little slower with `ts/all-MiniLM-L12-v2` but it did not actually get stuck). I've now tried this on a few different datasets. Would you be able to share a sample dataset? 

As for recommendation on the best model, you can refer to the MTEB leaderboard to check how different models perform across a variety of domains and Q&A datsets: https://huggingface.co/spaces/mteb/leaderboard
